# WEB PROJECT RELEASE STANDARD (always apply)

Applies to every web project in `C:\Users\Administrator\Projects\IT-Agency`: sites, landings, shops, corporate, portfolio, SaaS, CRM with public frontend, Next.js/React/Vue and future web apps.

Full standard: `docs/WEB_PROJECT_RELEASE_STANDARD.md`  
Templates: `templates/web-project-compliance/`  
Init: `tools/init-web-project-compliance.ps1`

## Mandatory release gates

Do not treat a site as release-ready until applicable gates are done (via **own** code/architecture/business-flow analysis) and serious production projects have `docs/RELEASE_AUDIT.md` with a final verdict.

Required (when applicable):

1. Russian law applicability analysis
2. Personal data / 152-FZ
3. Privacy policy + consent (when consent is the basis / when PD collected)
4. Localization of primary PD collection (RF citizens)
5. Roskomnadzor notification assessment (owner action — never assert registration)
6. Cross-border transfer risks
7. Russian-language public information
8. Consumer protection (2300-1) when offering to consumers
9. Advertising (38-FZ) / ERID — only if real ads
10. Payments (54-FZ) — only if payment + receipt duty
11. Security baseline
12. SEO baseline (Cursor performs this; tools do not replace it)
13. Accessibility baseline
14. Technical quality (build/tests/live checks when domain exists)
15. **Client / Owner Actions** recommendations (mandatory deliverable)

First determine **applicability**. Do not mechanically apply every law to every site.

## Optional supporting tools (NOT mandatory)

**PR-CY** (`https://pr-cy.ru/`) = OPTIONAL SUPPORTING TOOL  
**Auditikk** (`https://auditikk.ru/`) = OPTIONAL SUPPORTING TOOL

Use when: public production domain exists; extra independent automated audit helps; project-specific value; client asks; agent judges it useful.

Do NOT: require for every site; treat absence as blocker; treat reports as legal opinions; use tool scores as primary readiness criterion; buy paid plans without explicit user permission.

PR-CY does not replace SEO audit. Auditikk does not replace legal/security audit.

## Status vocabulary (mandatory)

`PASS` | `NOT APPLICABLE` | `NEEDS OWNER DATA` | `NEEDS OWNER ACTION` | `NEEDS REVIEW` | `NEEDS LEGAL REVIEW` | `BLOCKED`

`BLOCKED` only when the issue truly prevents safe/lawful launch of a specific function or production mode.

Final verdict ONLY: `READY FOR TECHNICAL RELEASE` | `READY WITH OWNER ACTIONS` | `NEEDS REVIEW` | `BLOCKED`

Never write `PRODUCTION READY` if any item is `BLOCKED`.  
Never claim full legal compliance from automated checks. Automated audit ≠ legal opinion.

## Never invent owner/legal data

Do NOT invent: ИНН, ОГРН/ОГРНИП, FIO, ООО/ИП, address, bank details, Roskomnadzor number, licenses, certificates, real reviews, guarantees, prices, owner phone/email, legal status.

Missing → `NEEDS OWNER DATA`. If mandatory for the release mode → may escalate to `BLOCKED`.

## Russian law baseline (as of work date)

1. **152-FZ** — if PD collected/processed  
2. Separate consent when consent is the legal basis (incl. rules requiring separation from other confirmations)  
3. Privacy policy reflecting real processing  
4. Roskomnadzor notification — owner decision  
5. Localization of primary collection for RF citizens  
6. Cross-border transfers  
7. Russian-language public information (incl. rules from 01.03.2026 where applicable)  
8. **2300-1** — if consumer offers  
9. **38-FZ** / ERID — only if real advertising  
10. **54-FZ** — only if payments + receipt duty  
11. Industry rules — if project requires  

## Personal data / cookies

Map forms/fields, purposes, bases, storage, retention, recipients, processors. Consent (if used): not pre-checked; explicit action; policy link; separated when required; matches code. PD collected → `/privacy` (or equivalent) with real operator/processing facts. Never invent operator data.

Cookies: inventory ESSENTIAL/ANALYTICS/MARKETING/FUNCTIONAL/OTHER. Non-essential after required consent. Essential-only → no pointless complex banner.

## Client / Owner Actions (mandatory output)

For each site, produce project-specific **CLIENT / OWNER ACTIONS**: what cannot be done by coding alone (legal status, ИНН, address, RKN notice, retention, real prices/reviews/photos, offer if needed, online cash register if needed, ad marking if needed, etc.). Do not paste a generic identical list for every project — derive from actual flow.

Also record: Owner Data Required, Legal Review Required, Blockers.

## Technical audit (Cursor, mandatory independently)

HTTPS, redirects, robots, sitemap, canonical, metadata, headings, indexability, broken links, Schema (factual only — no fake ratings), OG, performance, mobile, a11y, forms, validation, cookies, security headers, authz, dependency vulns, secrets, production config.

Security/SEO/a11y baselines remain mandatory regardless of optional tools.

## RELEASE_AUDIT.md

Required for serious production web projects. Core sections: Legal applicability, PD/152-FZ, Consent, Privacy, Roskomnadzor, Localization, Cross-border, Russian Language, Consumer Protection, Advertising, Payments, Security, SEO, Accessibility, External Services, Client/Owner Actions, Owner Data Required, Legal Review Required, Blockers, Final Verdict.

Optional section: Additional Automated Audits (PR-CY / Auditikk = NOT RUN | RUN). Absence must not change Final Verdict if mandatory gates were completed otherwise.

## Agent behavior

- Analyze actual code + architecture + business flow; update audit when facts change.
- New web project: `tools/init-web-project-compliance.ps1 -ProjectPath ...`
- Nested repos need their own copy of this rule.
- No deploy/push/production restart/DB migration unless user asks.
- Sales Agent production: no runtime/.env/scheduler/systemd/DB/deploy changes unless asked.
- Never print secrets from `.env*` / credentials / keys / tokens.
